From 1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.org>
Date: Sat, 01 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: sun5i-r8-chip: enable NAND controller

Enable the NAND Flash Controller (NFC) on the C.H.I.P. board by adding
a DTS node with the correct pinctrl groups and hardware ECC settings.

The CHIP uses a Hynix or Toshiba MLC NAND connected to the NFC.  The
controller is defined in sun5i.dtsi but left disabled; this overlay
enables it with the standard CHIP pinmux (nand_pins, nand_cs0, nand_rb0)
and hardware BCH ECC, matching the configuration used by the Linux kernel
DTS for the CHIP.

Without this node the DM NAND driver (sunxi_nand.c) does not probe,
making nand/ubi/ubifsmount/ubifsload U-Boot shell commands unavailable
at runtime even when CONFIG_NAND_SUNXI=y.  Note that the SPL NAND reader
(sunxi_nand_spl.c) is register-based and works without a DTS node.

Signed-off-by: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.org>
---
 arch/arm/dts/sun5i-r8-chip.dts | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/sun5i-r8-chip.dts b/arch/arm/dts/sun5i-r8-chip.dts
index 1a2b3c4..5d6e7f8 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/sun5i-r8-chip.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/sun5i-r8-chip.dts
@@ -280,3 +280,15 @@
 	usb0_vbus-supply = <&reg_usb0_vbus>;
 	usb1_vbus-supply = <&reg_vcc5v0>;
 };
+
+&nfc {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&nand_pins &nand_cs0_pin &nand_rb0_pin>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	nand@0 {
+		reg = <0>;
+		allwinner,rb = <0>;
+		nand-ecc-mode = "hw";
+	};
+};
